			<h2 id="post-685"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2007/07/binding-to-the-byte-of-an-image-in-wpf/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Binding to an Image Byte[] in WPF">Binding to an Image Byte[] in WPF</a></h2>
			<small class="meta">July 26th, 2007 </small>

			<div class="entry">
				<p>I&#8217;m working on a&nbsp;WPF app for my wife who coaches our local high school track team.&nbsp; One of the features she wanted was to have some images for different players and teams and, religious debate aside, I have chosen to save these in SQL Server 2005.&nbsp; I&#8217;m using <a href="http://www.hibernate.org/343.html" mce_href="http://www.hibernate.org/343.html">NHibernate</a>&nbsp;for all my data access which has been a great experience (my first).&nbsp; Impressively, NHibernate supports SQL Server <i>Image</i> columns via the inherent <i>Byte[]&nbsp;</i> type (See Section 5.1.9 of the <a href="http://www.hibernate.org/hib_docs/nhibernate/html/mapping.html" mce_href="http://www.hibernate.org/hib_docs/nhibernate/html/mapping.html">docs</a>).&nbsp; This made adding the Image to my classes <b>very</b> easy.&nbsp; </p>
<p>Here&#8217;s a snippet of my class with the corresponding NHibernate Mapping Xml File:</p>
